Call log (`/tmp/rl-rehearsal-calls-t19.log`): exactly 3 lines, all `review` calls, scenario `ok`, models `gpt-6-luna`, `gpt-6-luna`, `muse-ember-1.0`; no `repair` line; no model was started (the `claude` on `PATH` was the fake).
Run folder `RL/runs/rehearsal-rl-final/` holds `run.json`, `timing.json`, `check/check.json`, `merged/merged-1.md`; the merged report holds 0 occurrences of each of `probe`, `src`, `class`, `ledger-v1`; `run.json`: `fallback: false`, `check_skipped: false`, `reask: []`.

Addendum, written during Task 20 (a defect of this build's process, found and corrected): `RL/runs/rehearsal-rl-final/run.json` holds `freeze_tag: "rl-freeze-094c1a314886"`.
Cause: during the Task 18 review a reviewer sub-session ran `bin/freeze.sh` without `--no-write` and left `RL/config/freeze.json` (modified 03:29:52); `run-panel.sh` reads `freeze_tag` from that file and the Task 19 rehearsal ran with it present. The tag was never created (`git tag -l` is identical to the list taken before Task 18).
`bin/freeze.sh` states that no `config/freeze.json` may exist before the real freeze, so the stray file was removed (a copy is in `/tmp/rl-t19/stray-freeze.json`), and the rehearsal was run again on the clean tree with a new run id:
`bash $RL/bin/run-panel.sh --arm RL --panel primary --doc TASK-WF-designSpec-20261107-075614 --replicate 1 --block 1 --seed 1 --run-id rehearsal-rl-clean` (fake claude first on `PATH`, `FAKE_SCENARIO=ok`, `FAKE_CALL_LOG=/tmp/rl-rehearsal-calls-clean.log`)
-> `run rehearsal-rl-clean: arm=RL panel=primary fallback=0 check_skipped=0 merged=3 merge_exit=0 elapsed_s=1.438`, exit code 0; call log: 3 lines, all `review` (`muse-ember-1.0`, `gpt-6-luna`, `gpt-6-luna`); `run.json` has `freeze_tag: null`, `fallback: false`, `check_skipped: false`, `reask: []`; the merged report holds 0 occurrences of `probe`, `src`, `class`, `ledger-v1`.
The folder `runs/rehearsal-rl-final/` is kept as it was written and is not the clean evidence for the missing freeze; `runs/rehearsal-rl-clean/` is.

